## Task 1 — Cohere AI stock recommendations API route
Create app/api/recommendations/route.ts:

- Method: POST
- Body: { session_id: string }
- Fetch the user's watchlist from Supabase:
  select ticker, company_name, sector, status 
  from watchlist where session_id = $1
- If the watchlist is empty return:
  { recommendations: [], message: "Add some stocks to your portfolio first" }
- Build a prompt:
  "The user has these stocks in their portfolio:
  [list each stock as: TICKER - Company Name (Sector) - Status]
  Based on their investment interests and sectors, recommend 3 stocks 
  they might want to research next.
  For each recommendation provide: ticker, name, reason (2 sentences max).
  Respond only with a JSON array, no markdown, no backticks:
  [{ "ticker": string, "name": string, "reason": string }]"
- Call Cohere API using native fetch:
  POST https://api.cohere.com/v2/chat
  Headers:
    Authorization: Bearer process.env.COHERE_API_KEY
    Content-Type: application/json
  Body:
  {
    "model": "command-r",
    "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": prompt }]
  }
- Parse response: data.message.content[0].text
- JSON.parse that text to get array of { ticker, name, reason }
- Return { recommendations }
- On any error return { recommendations: [], error: string } with status 500
- Use createClient directly with env vars for Supabase
- Use native fetch for Cohere — no SDK

